Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:37:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 151/160] hjviewer: review fixes for the desktop settings split

- Advanced settings rebuilds on each visit again. The network block and
  the security cards kept upstream's keep-alive inside the page's list,
  and from there it held the whole page in the settings' PageView: after
  a change on another tab (the Display tab's image quality preset) the
  page went on showing the value it had. Neither keeps the page alive
  now; the unlocks are the settings page's, so they last as before. The
  Security tab keeps its keep-alive. As the page may now be gone when an
  unlock's permission check returns, its two unlock buttons rebuild it
  only while it is there.
- The security group is the page's last: the audio input and the privacy
  mode implementation, which no unlock holds, come first, then the
  Security unlock and only cards it holds. The service and updates group
  (whose update rows a pinned build fixes, so they are grey either way)
  comes before it.
- Titles from upstream's keys: the session defaults card is "Other
  Default Options", as the Display tab's card with the other three of
  those options; the security card plain "Security"; the custom image
  quality card "Custom Image Quality". The Display tab's "Custom
  (advanced settings)" line shows as the selected value, greyed only
  when fixed. ko.rs keeps three new keys, beside HJViewer's own two
  ("Update failed!") instead of at the end, where upstream's
  translation syncs append.
- Tests read desktop_setting_page.dart and desktop_home_page.dart: the
  tabs (no Network tab), the everyday tabs' rows, the groups' order with
  their cards, and the home's "Change ID" opening Advanced settings.

Known limits: the home's "Change ID" opens Advanced settings at its top,
and the ID card is the page's last; scrolling to it would need a handle
into the page and a post-frame callback. At the next upstream update,
rows upstream adds to the General tab's other() or the Security tab's
more() need their place (an everyday tab or Advanced settings) chosen by
hand: a clean merge leaves them in whichever of the split functions
their neighbours went to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
